A||N||1||Cozmo||Gear ratio math? (convoluted version)||||5||
Z||000000||Cozmo||07-05-2001||07:45 AM||||While shooting the breeze over brews with some other Fiero owners after a road trip last week we got to talking about RPM /MPH differences.<BR>  It seems my '85 4sp. 2M6 Targa runs at 3600 RPM at 60 MPH.  So I got out my handy dandy calculator to run some numbers, here's what I came up with:<BR>(BTW I'm no Steven Hawking by a LOONG shot so beware... some flawed math ahead fer shure... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<P>OK...<BR>First, how many times the tire turns each 60 miles traveled.<BR>Tire diameter is 25.875 in.  That gives a tire circumference of 81.3 in.<BR>There are 63,360 inches in a mile.  That means the tire revolves 779.34 times per mile, so in one hour at 60MPH it revolves 46,760.4 times.<P>Now the engine revolves 3600 times per min., or 216,000 times per hour.<P>Put these together and we get:<BR>(#engine revs per hour @60MPH) divided by (#wheel revs per hour @60MPH) equals (effective differential final drive ratio)<BR>OR<BR>(216,000)/(46,760.4)=4.62.<P>OK<BR><B>????  4.62 ?????</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>I know there are some real "fudge factors" involved here, especially speedo and tach calibration. But this still confirms my suspicion that the previous owner put in a 4.10 out of an '84. (figure a +/- 15% on my "math").<P>No wonder that first gear is about useless! I guess this will never be my "long road trip car" but boy does it haul butt 0-60!<P><B>E-HAH!!!</B><BR>I guess I need to examine the trans. to see if it says "M-19" on it. Where is it located?<BR>Thanks, you people are GREAT!<P>C02M0<BR>   <P><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Will||07-05-2001||10:25 AM||||I don't see anything wrong with your math.<P>Do you drive in third?<BR>With a 0.85 4th, a 4.10 should give an overall ratio of 3.485.<P>4.62/4.1 = 1.13  Isn't that close to third in your trans?||||reg||1
